Inquiry — shared ways to understand and investigate (@inquiry-map: 0, is #chapter, #inquiry "quantitative-literacy/Quantitative-literacy.lingua#r_4XVN56PQC13JGNFPV0CSGXDCZ2", #inquiry "metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5", #inquiry "reproducible-computation/Reproducible-computation.lingua#r_78FWWJDCV0ZGG7VYSPRCWN56DQ") { r_75MNKZQKNB0XBG021SWWW2HASB
Begin with a question, make the terms and quantities explicit, examine the reasons or observations, and revise the answer when the evidence changes. These practices connect learning across fields.

[Quantitative and technical literacy](quantitative-literacy/Quantitative-literacy.lingua#r_4XVN56PQC13JGNFPV0CSGXDCZ2) begins from arithmetic and develops drawings, balances, measurement, and advanced model reasoning through substantial books and practical studies. Use the shared Records wherever a scientific, engineering, or production question needs them.

[Measurement and metrology](metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5) reuses that preparation and develops quantity definitions, calibration, reference chains, uncertainty, physical measurement families, laboratory comparisons, and demanding practical and scholarly investigations.

[Reproducible computational work](reproducible-computation/Reproducible-computation.lingua#r_78FWWJDCV0ZGG7VYSPRCWN56DQ) begins with a saved calculation and develops programming, data meaning, independent checks, versioning, environment reconstruction, workflows, numerical and stochastic validation, resources, preservation, and substantial computational research.

Connect the question with [Philosophy](../philosophy/Philosophy.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001001), [STEM](../stem/STEM.lingua#r_4B137J3ZBVM7TD2NA797H2CZ7E), and [Ergon](../ergon/Ergon.lingua#r_00000000000000000000002001). These are entrances into the same connected knowledge; following another reference does not change a selected learning sequence's boundary.
} r_75MNKZQKNB0XBG021SWWW2HASB

